Privacy Policy

Effective: 27 September 2026

Hermbro uses Google OAuth to provide Google Workspace functionality through Hermes Agent.

When authorized, Hermbro may access Google Workspace data such as Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Contacts, Sheets, and Docs, depending on the permissions granted by the user.

Google user data is used only to provide functionality explicitly requested by the user. It is not sold, used for advertising, or used to train generalized AI or machine-learning models.

Authentication credentials and OAuth tokens are stored on systems controlled by the operator. Google data may be processed by service providers when necessary to perform a user-requested function.

Users can revoke Google access at any time through their Google Account.

Hermbro's use of information received from Google Workspace APIs adheres to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including its Limited Use requirements.

